{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "open-audit",
  "description": "One page of the devices collection with the per-device include=ip,network read that supplies MACs. Proves the cookie login is exchanged at /index.php/logon and replayed as a Cookie header on the data calls, that the JSON:API envelope's data[].attributes is where the device lives, and that the included block is walked as an object keyed by table name. Device 14 exercises the address/adapter join: the ip and network rows are married on net_index, the docker0 bridge is recognised as a software adapter so neither its MAC nor its address reaches the asset, and an adapter with a MAC but no bound address still becomes an interface because a MAC is the strongest merge signal a switch port ever sees. Device 27 is SNMP-discovered and returns included as an empty PHP array rather than an object, which is the type variance that would abort a run that subscripted it blindly; its only address is the one on the device row. Device 42 proves the placeholder filters: 'To Be Filled By O.E.M.' never becomes a serial, 'localhost' never becomes a hostname, and the 169.254 address the host invented when DHCP failed is dropped even though the platform itself keeps link-local.",
